== what goes on the wire ==
compressed frame sets RSV1 true
compressed frame is a binary frame true
compressed frame is final true
64 KiB of repetition leaves under a kilobyte true
the payload does not end in the sync marker true
context takeover makes the repeat smaller true
an empty message is one 0x00 byte true
a second empty message is one 0x00 byte true
a ping is uncompressed true
a pong is uncompressed true
a close frame is uncompressed true
no context takeover repeats the same bytes true
no context takeover is worse than takeover true
a 32 KiB window crushes 4 KiB-apart repeats true
a 512-byte window cannot reach them true
without the extension nothing is compressed true
an 8-bit window is refused at the API true
== what a server accepts ==
one compressed text frame: got [text:hello compressed world,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
a compressed message across two frames: got [text:hello compressed world,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
a compressed message across three frames: got [text:hello compressed world,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
RSV1 on a continuation frame: got [] error=1 close=1002 answered_extension=true
RSV1 on a ping: got [] error=1 close=1002 answered_extension=true
RSV1 with no extension: got [] error=1 close=1002 answered_extension=false
an uncompressed message on a compressed connection: got [text:plain,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
compressed, plain, compressed: got [text:hello compressed world,text:plain,text:hello compressed world,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
a payload that is not DEFLATE: got [] error=1 close=1007 answered_extension=true
a compressed empty message: got [text:,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
compressed text that is not UTF-8: got [] error=1 close=1007 answered_extension=true
compressed text with multi-byte UTF-8: got [text:héllo — wörld ✓,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
an empty compressed payload, then a real one: got [text:,text:hello compressed world,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
two messages that each end their DEFLATE stream: got [text:a message in a final block,text:a message in a final block,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
a megabyte of zeros fits in a small frame true
a megabyte claimed by a kilobyte: got [] error=2 close=1009 answered_extension=true
the same bomb under a limit that allows it: got [binary:1048576,closed:1000] error=0 close=1000 answered_extension=true
== both ends are the library ==
permessage-deflate -> clean true
permessage-deflate; server_no_context_takeover -> clean true
permessage-deflate; client_no_context_takeover -> clean true
permessage-deflate; server_no_context_takeover; client_no_context_takeover -> clean true
permessage-deflate; server_max_window_bits=9 -> clean true
permessage-deflate; client_max_window_bits=9 -> clean true
permessage-deflate; server_no_context_takeover; server_max_window_bits=9 -> clean true
permessage-deflate; server_no_context_takeover; client_no_context_takeover; server_max_window_bits=9; client_max_window_bits=9 -> clean true
== the handshake, end to end ==
with compression: agreed=permessage-deflate refused=too_large clean=true
without compression: agreed=(none) refused=too_large clean=true
